  "notes": [
    "The PDF holds two forms: page 1 is the FDP Form 10b Goods and Services bid-out (Fourth Quarter CY 2019); page 2 is a Civil Works form for 4th Quarter CY 2019 (its header still reads \"FDP Form 10b - Bid Results on Goods and Services\"). Page 2 signatories: Cleofe A. Amores (BAC Secretariat Head) and Atty. James Allan Sayson (BAC Chairperson).",
    "goodsServices 19-10-2149 (Water Storage Tank Rain Collector, INCA PHILS. INC.): the Bid Amount cell is blank on the form.",
    "goodsServices 19-10-2109 (Meals): printed bid 909,650.00 exceeds the printed ABC 711,500.00; transcribed as printed (the same figure appears as a bid amount in the Q1 2019 form).",
    "goodsServices 19-10-2283 (Textbooks): printed bid 4,195,000.00 exceeds the printed ABC 4,159,000.00 (possible digit transposition on the form); transcribed as printed.",
    "goodsServices 19-10-2373: bidding date printed \"26-Mar-19\" although all other rows are Nov-Dec 2019; transcribed as printed.",
    "Spellings kept as printed: \"Purified Rabiew Vaccines\", \"J-Joel Enteprises & Printing\", \"Punta Pricesa\", \"Stepehen Philip C. Arquisola\", \"108 F Lamas St.\".",
    "civilWorks 19-17A: a pen mark overlaps the bidding date; read as \"Dec. 15, 2019\".",
    "civilWorks: the \"Name and Address Of Bidder\" column prints a contact person above the address; split into bidderContact and bidderAddress.",
    "bidderNormalized: a canonical spelling added by the transcriber so the same company ranks as one bidder across documents (case, punctuation and obvious misspellings unified, e.g. variants confirmed by the bidder name repeated in the address column or by an identical contact person/address). The printed name is kept unchanged in bidder."
